{{Quote|Imperial loyalists condemned the Free Ryloth movement after outlaw Cham Syndulla claimed responsibility for a reservoir explosion that washed away an Imperial hovertrain.|A report in the TriNebulon News|<ref name="Rebel Files" />}}
'''Hovertrains''',<ref name="Levels">{{InsiderCite|151|One Thousand Levels Down}}</ref> also known as '''mag-levs''',<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> or '''repulsor trains''',<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> were vehicles used in mass-transit that operated by hovering. Such trains operated on planets such as [[Coruscant]]<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> and [[Ryloth]]. During the [[Ryloth Insurgency|insurgency]] on [[Ryloth]], [[Cham Syndulla]] and his [[Free Ryloth Movement|resistance fighters]] [[Imperial hovertrain attack|attacked]] a reservoir that swept away an Imperial hovertrain. The attack was later condemned by [[Governor]] [[Pommel (Governor)|Pommel]] on the [[TriNebulon News]].<ref name="Rebel Files" />

In the [[New Republic Era]], a [[Tatooine repulsor train|hovertrain]] was also used by the [[Pyke Syndicate]] as a way of transporting [[spice]] from the [[spice mines of Kessel]] across the deserts of [[Tatooine]] until it eventually got hijacked by a clan of [[Tusken Raider]]s with the help of [[Boba Fett]].<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

{{Veh-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Hovertrains are mentioned in the short story "[[One Thousand Levels Down]]," published in [[Star Wars Insider 151|''Star Wars Insider'' 151]].

